.Sh STANDARDS
Linux's KVM API, version 12, for x86, as its
.Pa Documentation/virt/kvm/api.rst
gives it.
.Sh BUGS
At most 64 vCPUs in a VM, with ids below 256, and 256 memory slots.
No in-kernel PIC, I/O APIC or PIT, no routes but MSI and SINT routes, no
irqfd resample, no
.Dv KVM_CAP_X2APIC_API ,
no coalesced MMIO, no dirty ring, no SMM and no nested virtualization, so
no enlightened VMCS and no direct TLB flush of Hyper-V's.
The APIC timer is checked at each entry, and the host's tick of 1 ms
makes the guest exit, so an expiry reaches the guest within a tick.
